    "name": "finetune-blur-freeze-cpu",
    "description": "Task 9.6: 9.5's recipe (finetune-blur-cpu.yaml, D36) with exactly one change, the backbone frozen (Ultralytics `freeze: 11`: layers 0 to 10 of YOLO11n, the convolutional backbone, SPPF and C2PSA), so only the neck and the Detect head adapt. Picked before running (D39): 9.5's no-blur control lost 3 to 6 points on every condition (E-061), which points at forgetting in 800 COCO images for 80 classes; of the two candidate changes, the warmup's high bias learning rate is already off under the automatic AdamW optimizer (Ultralytics 8.4.175 sets warmup_bias_lr to 0 for Adam), so dropping warmup would change only a 3-epoch ramp, while freezing keeps the pretrained features that the forgetting hypothesis says are being overwritten. Everything else is 9.5's: training list v1, seed, 10 epochs, batch 16, imgsz 640, no mosaic, last epoch kept, a blur-mix run and a no-blur control, the same eval (detection subset v1 clean, blur 3 and 6, noise 25; COCO and MOT17; paired bootstrap).\n",
